## 2026-07-02 (cont. 2)
_User reported "clicking the AI narration button does nothing" after the chip-as-player rewrite. Ran it down with a real headless Chromium (installed playwright chromium + system libs in the throwaway container): the click DOES land on the toggle (hit-test hits .post-listen-lead), NO JS errors, handler fires — jsdom also confirms is-playing/label toggle. The only failure was audio.play() rejecting with MediaError code 4 (FFmpegDemuxer "data source error") which is a chromium-HEADLESS-SHELL Opus limitation, NOT a real bug: ffmpeg decodes the file cleanly (Ogg Opus, 476s, exit 0), WEBrick serves it 200 + honors Range (206), and canPlayType returns "probably". So the player code is functionally correct and audio plays in a real browser. User said to stop chasing it ("super not important, go with what we have"). Left the chip-as-player as-is. Still uncommitted. If it ever misbehaves for real, likely a stale/cached page — hard refresh._

