_Got the real giscus comment DOM from the user. Key facts: giscus puts `color-box-border-info` on the OUTER comment wrapper (div.gsc-comment>div) for OWNER comments (not just the pill), so `:has(.color-box-border-info)` matches — bubble-right worked (merged PR #22, now in main). But the header stayed left because avatar/name/time/pill live in a full-width `.gsc-comment-author` flex row inside `.gsc-comment-header`; aligning the header alone doesn't move a full-width child. Fix (PR #23, branch fix/giscus-owner-header): right-pack inside `.gsc-comment-author` via justify-content:flex-end + width:100% + text-align:right fallback. DOM ref also: wrapper classes `color-bg-primary w-full min-w-0 rounded-md border color-box-border-info`; content `.markdown.gsc-comment-content`; reply box `.gsc-reply-box`. Reminded user theme changes are deploy-gated; suggested devtools live-edit of the giscus iframe to preview CSS before committing (avoids merge-to-test round trips)._
